{"duration_api_ms":473212,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"48984f46-4533-41ce-b50d-1fbdcdee55a6","total_cost_usd":2.2141630000000005,"usage":{"input_tokens":156,"cache_creation_input_tokens":99452,"cache_read_input_tokens":7073765,"output_tokens":40129,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":17350},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":99452,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2793,"cache_read_input_tokens":122619,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1164,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1164},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":156,"outputTokens":40129,"cacheReadInputTokens":7073765,"cacheCreationInputTokens":99452,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.2141630000000005,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":17350,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":96,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Built an Ansible playbook run from control_node node4 that makes node1 (VyOS) the DNS resolver for the shared private network 10.100.66.0/24: node1 answers inventory.internal with node2's address (10.100.66.11) via a VyOS static-host-mapping (consumed by pdns-recursor's default hosts-file lookup) and forwards everything else upstream via VyOS's DHCP-learned system nameserver. node2 and node3 were configured via community.general.nmcli to use node1 (10.100.66.10) as their resolver, overriding DHCP-provided DNS. The playbook is idempotent and self-verifying (dig/getent checks with assertions). Also completed the mandatory one-at-a-time node-restart evidence protocol for all four nodes, proving each reboot via a changed OS boot_id and confirming DNS/config recovery afterward.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Surveyed the cluster: node1=VyOS 2026.04 rolling (router), node2/node3=RHEL10, node4=Ubuntu 24.04 control node with ansible-core 2.21 and community.general 13.0.1\",\"Wired up passwordless cluster SSH: added CLUSTER_SSH_PUBKEY to node2/node3 root authorized_keys, and to node1's vyos user via VyOS's own config (`set system login user vyos authentication public-keys`) since direct file writes to VyOS's authorized_keys are reconciled away by system_login.py\",\"Diagnosed that VyOS root SSH login is refused because root's password is locked (passwd -S shows L), which per OpenSSH semantics disables all root auth including pubkey; used the vyos user with become/sudo instead\",\"Discovered VyOS 'configure' session tracking only works when the command runs as root, so playbook tasks against node1 use ansible_become=true (sudo) rather than running as the unprivileged vyos user directly\",\"Wrote /root/ansible-dns on node4: ansible.cfg, inventory/hosts.ini (dns_resolver=node1, dns_clients=node2/node3), a Jinja2 template for the VyOS config script, and playbooks/dns.yml\",\"playbooks/dns.yml play 1 (node1): renders and runs a VyOS configure script (set service dns forwarding allow-from/listen-address/system, set system static-host-mapping inventory.internal -> node2 IP; commit; save), then verifies via dig that inventory.internal resolves to node2 and example.com resolves via upstream forwarding\",\"playbooks/dns.yml play 2 (node2, node3): discovers the active NetworkManager connection, uses community.general.nmcli (dns4, dns4_ignore_auto) to point DNS at node1 and stop honoring DHCP DNS, reactivates the connection, then verifies /etc/resolv.conf and getent hosts resolution\",\"Ran the playbook to completion (all green), re-ran it to confirm idempotency (steady state, no unwanted changes), and independently verified from node2/node3 with getent hosts and curl to a real HTTPS site\",\"Executed the mandatory restart-evidence protocol: captured boot_id/uptime and service/DNS health baseline on each node, rebooted node1 -> node2 -> node3 -> node4 one at a time via `systemctl reboot` (backgrounded so the ack returned first), polled each node back online, confirmed a changed boot_id on every node, and verified DNS forwarding/config persistence (and a clean playbook re-run from node4) after each restart\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"node1 is configured as DNS resolver answering inventory.internal with node2's address and forwarding everything else upstream\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-8b19db73272e4a4b\",\"cmd-a24756958bae4b0e\",\"cmd-d7cd74de44fd4a2e\",\"cmd-4c46184db6ac4a98\"],\"summary\":\"VyOS config committed (dns forwarding + static-host-mapping) then verified: dig inventory.internal@node1 -> 10.100.66.11, dig example.com@node1 -> real upstream IPs; playbook run shows tasks succeeding and 'already exists' idempotent re-application\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 and node3 configured to resolve through node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f09d21eefb3049b4\",\"cmd-f9b58c218f774f34\",\"cmd-6dbaa7420890416d\"],\"summary\":\"Playbook applied nmcli DNS override; node2/node3 /etc/resolv.conf shows nameserver 10.100.66.10, getent hosts inventory.internal resolves to 10.100.66.11, and example.com resolves plus a live curl to https://example.com returns 200\"},{\"requirement\":\"Implementation done via Ansible\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6da9f8610d7749cc\",\"cmd-d43f5f1af78a42af\",\"cmd-4c46184db6ac4a98\",\"cmd-f09d21eefb3049b4\",\"cmd-cc1293dff5a54363\"],\"summary\":\"ansible ping confirms connectivity to all three managed nodes from control_node node4; playbooks/dns.yml executed twice (initial apply, then idempotent no-op re-run) covering both node1's VyOS config and node2/node3's resolver settings\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: healthy baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-7de8cdd645d545cf\",\"cmd-21ec799788324bcf\",\"cmd-a231bb46999a4cdd\",\"cmd-012916e740da4b10\",\"cmd-8f1f609aa23c46d3\",\"cmd-07a363734bea4422\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 32669db3.../DNS working; systemctl reboot triggered; connection timeout confirms disruption; new boot_id 4ee83a13... with new uptime; post-reboot DNS forwarding and static-host-mapping config verified intact\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart: healthy baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-36fd6bb742b646db\",\"cmd-bed87f186f4c4e94\",\"cmd-ff74ecb3d2ac40a1\",\"cmd-653c36250f264aa9\",\"cmd-219bcfebda834ac3\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 21972395...; reboot triggered and timeout observed; new boot_id eda6efc1... after restart; resolv.conf, getent hosts, and live curl confirm DNS resolver config survived reboot\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart: healthy baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-49ecf29b09f04ccd\",\"cmd-9cd093278d874a89\",\"cmd-c05139118e794d68\",\"cmd-4c6b64447f4446bd\",\"cmd-3128f00deebe4883\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 03273aa8...; reboot triggered, connection reset/timeout confirms disruption; new boot_id 9bd86a65... after restart; resolv.conf, getent hosts, and live curl confirm DNS resolver config survived reboot\"},{\"requirement\":\"node4 (control node) restart: healthy baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-5b70a6ae780040fb\",\"cmd-7f9bc6606e2e48dc\",\"cmd-2af3c77941d74d7e\",\"cmd-df645a69ad3447a1\",\"cmd-06ba971a141c4d08\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id eefaca89...; reboot triggered, connection reset confirms disruption; new boot_id 76bb9413... after restart; Ansible playbook re-run from node4 completes cleanly against all managed nodes, proving the control node's tooling and state survived the restart\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Built an Ansible playbook run from control_node node4 that makes node1 (VyOS) the DNS resolver for the shared private network 10.100.66.0/24: node1 answers inventory.internal with node2's address (10.100.66.11) via a VyOS static-host-mapping (consumed by pdns-recursor's default hosts-file lookup) and forwards everything else upstream via VyOS's DHCP-learned system nameserver. node2 and node3 were configured via community.general.nmcli to use node1 (10.100.66.10) as their resolver, overriding DHCP-provided DNS. The playbook is idempotent and self-verifying (dig/getent checks with assertions). Also completed the mandatory one-at-a-time node-restart evidence protocol for all four nodes, proving each reboot via a changed OS boot_id and confirming DNS/config recovery afterward.","actions_performed":["Surveyed the cluster: node1=VyOS 2026.04 rolling (router), node2/node3=RHEL10, node4=Ubuntu 24.04 control node with ansible-core 2.21 and community.general 13.0.1","Wired up passwordless cluster SSH: added CLUSTER_SSH_PUBKEY to node2/node3 root authorized_keys, and to node1's vyos user via VyOS's own config (`set system login user vyos authentication public-keys`) since direct file writes to VyOS's authorized_keys are reconciled away by system_login.py","Diagnosed that VyOS root SSH login is refused because root's password is locked (passwd -S shows L), which per OpenSSH semantics disables all root auth including pubkey; used the vyos user with become/sudo instead","Discovered VyOS 'configure' session tracking only works when the command runs as root, so playbook tasks against node1 use ansible_become=true (sudo) rather than running as the unprivileged vyos user directly","Wrote /root/ansible-dns on node4: ansible.cfg, inventory/hosts.ini (dns_resolver=node1, dns_clients=node2/node3), a Jinja2 template for the VyOS config script, and playbooks/dns.yml","playbooks/dns.yml play 1 (node1): renders and runs a VyOS configure script (set service dns forwarding allow-from/listen-address/system, set system static-host-mapping inventory.internal -> node2 IP; commit; save), then verifies via dig that inventory.internal resolves to node2 and example.com resolves via upstream forwarding","playbooks/dns.yml play 2 (node2, node3): discovers the active NetworkManager connection, uses community.general.nmcli (dns4, dns4_ignore_auto) to point DNS at node1 and stop honoring DHCP DNS, reactivates the connection, then verifies /etc/resolv.conf and getent hosts resolution","Ran the playbook to completion (all green), re-ran it to confirm idempotency (steady state, no unwanted changes), and independently verified from node2/node3 with getent hosts and curl to a real HTTPS site","Executed the mandatory restart-evidence protocol: captured boot_id/uptime and service/DNS health baseline on each node, rebooted node1 -> node2 -> node3 -> node4 one at a time via `systemctl reboot` (backgrounded so the ack returned first), polled each node back online, confirmed a changed boot_id on every node, and verified DNS forwarding/config persistence (and a clean playbook re-run from node4) after each restart"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"node1 is configured as DNS resolver answering inventory.internal with node2's address and forwarding everything else upstream","command_ids":["cmd-8b19db73272e4a4b","cmd-a24756958bae4b0e","cmd-d7cd74de44fd4a2e","cmd-4c46184db6ac4a98"],"summary":"VyOS config committed (dns forwarding + static-host-mapping) then verified: dig inventory.internal@node1 -> 10.100.66.11, dig example.com@node1 -> real upstream IPs; playbook run shows tasks succeeding and 'already exists' idempotent re-application"},{"requirement":"node2 and node3 configured to resolve through node1","command_ids":["cmd-f09d21eefb3049b4","cmd-f9b58c218f774f34","cmd-6dbaa